# **All three anchored, and the middle one is why.** `node_modules/` unanchored matches a directory of
# that name at *any* depth, and `@viliha/vui-vue`'s build vendors `@internationalized/date` inside its
# own `dist/node_modules/.pnpm/...`. That rule excluded seven real files, so a clone installed a
# package whose Calendar could not resolve its own imports — while the tree it was cut from worked.
/node_modules/
/packages/*/node_modules/
/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.env*.local
.DS_Store
